Can you provide a detailed tutorial for a specific project?
Absolutely! Let's dive into a detailed tutorial for building a project with TanStack. How about we create a simple React application using TanStack Query for data fetching and state management? Here's a step-by-step guide:

Step 1: Set Up Your Project
Create a new React project using Create React App or Vite:

bash
npx create-react-app my-tanstack-app
cd my-tanstack-app
Install the necessary dependencies:

bash
npm install @tanstack/react-query axios
Step 2: Set Up TanStack Query
Create a QueryClient and wrap your application with QueryClientProvider in src/index.js:

javascript
import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom';
import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import App from './App';

const queryClient = new QueryClient();

ReactDOM.render(
  <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>
    <App />
  </QueryClientProvider>,
  document.getElementById('root')
);
Step 3: Create an API Service
Create a file src/api.js to define your API service using Axios:

javascript
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: 'https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com',
});

export const fetchTodos = async () => {
  const response = await api.get('/todos');
  return response.data;
};
Step 4: Fetch Data with TanStack Query
Create a component src/components/Todos.js to fetch and display data using TanStack Query:

javascript
import React from 'react';
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { fetchTodos } from '../api';

const Todos = () => {
  const { data, error, isLoading } = useQuery(['todos'], fetchTodos);

  if (isLoading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  if (error) return <div>Error: {error.message}</div>;

  return (
    <ul>
      {data.map(todo => (
        <li key={todo.id}>{todo.title}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
};

export default Todos;
Step 5: Use the Component in Your App
Update src/App.js to include the Todos component:

javascript
import React from 'react';
import Todos from './components/Todos';

const App = () => {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>My TanStack App</h1>
      <Todos />
    </div>
  );
};

export default App;
Step 6: Run Your Application
Start your development server:

bash
npm start
You should now see a list of todos fetched from the API displayed in your application. This tutorial covers the basics of setting up a React project with TanStack Query for data fetching and state management. You can further extend this project by adding more features, such as mutation for creating, updating, and deleting todos.

